honk: dynamic ECH sources and XHTTP download-peer ECH

Combined patch for the OpenWrt honk package, based on
Glassyiris/honk feat/native-api @ 8b6778ce. Two features:

1. Share links may carry a dynamic ECH source in the ech= parameter,
   ech=<qname>+<doh-url> (the + may arrive as %2B or as a literal '+',
   which form-decodes to a space; a bare ech=<qname> uses the
   bootstrap resolver). The ECHConfigList is fetched via DoH (H2 POST,
   application/dns-message, HTTPS RR) when a connection is made,
   cached per source with TTL, and stays fail-open like ech=1. Static
   ech_config / ech_config_path take priority. A DoH fetch that
   receives ECH_REJECTED retry configs publishes them into the same
   cache for the next dial.

2. XHTTP downloadSettings accepts tlsSettings.echConfigList for the
   download peer: a base64 value is a static ECHConfigList, a
   <qname>[+<doh-url>] value is a dynamic source. The download peer
   no longer dials with a plaintext SNI when so configured; upload
   ECH is still never inherited.

Source commits (Glassyiris/honk feat/native-api branch
feat/ech-doh-source):
  e55d2a9b feat(config): store ech=<qname>+<doh-url> share-link source on TlsOptions
  21147490 feat(outbound): fetch ECHConfigList via DoH at connect time
  4c10c445 docs: document ech=<qname>+<doh-url> share-link form
  70dc7cc9 feat(config): accept echConfigList in XHTTP downloadSettings
  cfb61ddc docs: document echConfigList for XHTTP download peers

Apply with: patch -p1 < 0001-ech-doh-source.patch
(PKG_SOURCE_VERSION must be 8b6778ce for this patch to apply cleanly.)

